WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.800 --> 00:00:05.211
Your product asks an LLM thousands of small questions, every hour.

2
00:00:05.400 --> 00:00:08.933
Which intent is this? Is it an attack? Which button next?

3
00:00:09.100 --> 00:00:14.048
Each call takes about 1.4 seconds, and is billed. Most are repeats.

4
00:00:14.600 --> 00:00:18.143
shad0w is a learned shortcut for those repeat decisions.

5
00:00:18.500 --> 00:00:20.528
It watches your LLM's answers.

6
00:00:21.000 --> 00:00:24.374
It learns a small table. No GPU, no labels.

7
00:00:24.800 --> 00:00:32.514
Then it proves, on answers it never saw, where it agrees. At most 5% disagreement, at 90% confidence.

8
00:00:33.000 --> 00:00:36.345
There, shad0w answers in 2.4 microseconds.

9
00:00:36.600 --> 00:00:40.658
Everything else goes to your LLM, and becomes new training data.

10
00:00:41.600 --> 00:00:47.032
The same loop works on text, images, video frames, web pages and live streams.

11
00:00:52.600 --> 00:00:56.214
A bank app routes "my card was stolen" in microseconds.

12
00:00:56.400 --> 00:01:04.697
On eight support intents, it answered 94.3% of messages, agreeing 97.2% of the time.

13
00:01:05.200 --> 00:01:09.174
Stores tag tickets and products. Safety teams filter spam.

14
00:01:09.600 --> 00:01:14.650
AI apps block known prompt attacks. shad0w never allows anything on its own.

15
00:01:15.100 --> 00:01:19.397
A web agent replays a repeat errand with zero LLM calls.

16
00:01:26.800 --> 00:01:32.121
On three public datasets, it answered 61 to 86% of the traffic.

17
00:01:32.600 --> 00:01:36.595
One line of Python. Or zero: change your base URL.

18
00:01:37.000 --> 00:01:40.847
It doesn't write text, and it needs about a thousand answers first.

19
00:01:41.400 --> 00:01:45.072
Your LLM for the new questions. shad0w for the repeats.
